  "weightedComparability": "Proposed180EC: eight legal/gateway/transnationalbusinesslaw courses60EC; eight business/economics/entrepreneurship courses60EC; two research/statistics/qualitativecourses15EC; two sociologycourses15EC; ethics,internationalrelations,persuasion22.5EC; PPD7.5EC. Only one7.5EC comparativeprivate-lawcourse directly anchors the defining private-law complex. Public/criminal/EU/international law are genuine but cannot substitute sustained family/succession/property-transfer/notarialtax/professionalregulation substance. Financialdecisionmaking/publiceconomics/venturecreation are not bankinglaw,estateplanning,taxdoctrineorincorporationlaw. This is a substantive weighting judgment, not degree equivalence or a matched-row quota.",
  "candidateAssessment": [
    {
      "label": "Private law, business & economic governance",
      "outcome": "not-defensible",
      "reason": "UCR offers useful comparative private law, public and international law, transnational business law, accounting and economics. The proposed programme nevertheless gives most of its legal weight to broad public/criminal/EU/international fields, with only one comparative private-law course. It does not sustain the family, succession, property-transfer, transaction-tax and notarial professional-rule sequence that defines Notarial Law. Adding finance, entrepreneurship or social methods does not repair that missing disciplinary substance. No complete defensible UCR programme is established; the finding does not depend on professional licensing or identical national-law coverage alone."
